activation	Print prompt	2026-10-28T02:01:20.3200937Z {"title": "BindNamedParameters should skip validation when function has varargs = ANY", "body": "## Problem\n\nWhen a table function is registered with `varargs = LogicalType::ANY`, it accepts any number of positional arguments. However, `BindNamedParameters` still validates named parameters against the function's `named_parameters` map and rejects any that aren't explicitly declared.\n\nThis makes it impossible to create a generic \"forward everything\" table function that accepts arbitrary named parameters \u2014 which is needed for the Airport extension's passthrough mode (forwarding SQL to a remote DuckDB).\n\n## Example\n\n```cpp\nTableFunction table_func({}, my_execute_fn, my_bind_fn, ...);\ntable_func.varargs = LogicalType::ANY;\n// No named_parameters declared\n```\n\n```sql\n-- This works (positional only):\nSELECT * FROM my_func('file.csv');\n\n-- This fails:\nSELECT * FROM my_func('file.csv', header:=true);\n-- Error: Invalid named parameter \"header\" for function my_func\n-- Function does not accept any named parameters.\n```\n\nThe bind function never gets a chance to handle `header:=true` because `BindNamedParameters` rejects it first.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nIn `src/planner/binder/tableref/bind_named_parameters.cpp`, skip validation when the function has `varargs = ANY`:\n\n```cpp\nvoid Binder::BindNamedParameters(named_parameter_type_map_t &types, named_parameter_map_t &values,\n                                 QueryErrorContext &error_context, string &func_name) {\n    for (auto &kv : values) {\n        auto entry = types.find(kv.first);\n        if (entry == types.end()) {\n            // If function accepts varargs ANY, allow any named parameter too\n            if (types.empty()) {\n                // No declared params \u2014 treat as passthrough, skip validation\n                continue;\n            }\n            // ... existing error handling ...\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Use case\n\nThe Airport extension (upstream source reference) attaches remote DuckDB instances. In passthrough mode, function calls should be forwarded as SQL to the remote. The remote DuckDB validates the params \u2014 the local binder shouldn't need to.\n\nSee: upstream reference: Query-farm/airport/pull/49"}
